  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Luk Fu (Six Tigers). Hakka Chinese, 3-4 players, 38-card money deck (Coins/Strings/Myriads/Tens). Deal 12 each. Win 6+ Fu (tricks or Aged Cards). Nines and certain Aces are Aged (unbeatable). Cards become Aged if highest remaining. Must follow suit; discard if void. Can lead singles/sets/sequences. Five Aces = instant win.',
    Player: "Welcome to Luk Fu! This traditional Hakka game uses a special 38-card money-suited deck. Win 6 'Fu' (tigers) to winâ€”earn them by taking tricks or holding 'Aged Cards' like the Nines. Watch for cards becoming Aged as play progresses! Can you master the Six Tigers?",
    objective: 'The objective is to win tricks with at least six cards. The player who first takes six can stop the game and claim immediate victory; if he plays on and another player takes six tricks, that player is the sole victor. If no one takes six tricks the hand is drawn and there are no payments.',
    gameplay: "1. **The Fu**: A 'Fu' is earned by winning a trick or holding an 'Aged Card'. 2. **Aged Cards**: Certain cards (Nines and specific Aces) are 'Aged' and cannot be beaten. Other cards can BECOME aged if they are the highest remaining card in their suit. 3. **Gameplay**: Must follow suit. If unable, you must discard face-down. 4. **Tsoh (Play)**: A player can declare they will 'Play' and take responsibility for all losses if they fail to reach the Fu target. 5. **Combinations**: You can lead a single card, a set (same rank), or a sequence. Opponents beat with the same type (Higher rank/Higher suit).",
    keyRules: [
      'Win 6+ Fu to win the hand.',
      'Fu earned by winning tricks or holding Aged Cards.',
      'Nines and certain Aces are Aged (unbeatable).',
      'Cards can become Aged if highest remaining in suit.',
      'Must follow suit; discard face-down if void.',
      'Can lead singles, sets, or sequences.',
      'Five Aces (Ng Fu Ha San) = immediate victory.',
      "'Tsoh' declaration: Commit to 6+ Fu or pay all losses.",
